{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/374923-am-i-imagining-things","id":374923,"title":"Am I imagining things?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-18T23:15:11-08:00","id":374923,"title":"Am I imagining things?","content":"I could have sworn that in one book, there were written Arcanoi that duplicated the physical disciplines of Kindred as well as Obfuscate for Risen. Am I wrong in this? Did I see it in a fever-laden dream or was it just plain hope?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T00:01:21-08:00","id":374948,"title":"","content":"The Risen book says Risen can learn the physical Disciplines + Obfuscate, but it doesn't represent them as Arcanoi. (The major theory on this capacity is that Risen and Kindred have reached similar effects by different means, but ultimately no-one knows for sure.<br /> <br /> Might be based on that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T09:40:43-08:00","id":378139,"title":"","content":"I always thought access to Celerity was somewhat inappropriate for a zombie-like reanimated body. (Fortitude and Potence made good sense, being driven by the vengeful ghost's unbending will.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:06:06-08:00","id":378149,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn I saw the rules in a book at some point. I know the book says they can learn them, but I thought I saw somewhere some Arcanoi to replicate those Disciplines.<br /> @Matt I am curious what makes you think that they are zombies? Sure, zombies do come back from the dead but they are usually mindless (unless you use Zombie the Coil...my favorite fan-splat for cWoD but that is neither here nor there) and there are also plenty of tales of people who have come back from the dead to avenge their deaths or else save their families in a corporeal form and not just as a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T10:37:05-08:00","id":378188,"title":"","content":"Absent their book, Risen got coverage in the Shadow Player's Guide and Guildbook: Pardoners and Puppeteers. Nothing on that score there. Eyeballing the Wraith books, I can't see anywhere else it would've appeared.<br /> <br /> Fan-work, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T17:39:39-08:00","id":378541,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it was. A fever-induced dream. I think I would still make some Arcanoi for anyone who wanted to play one at my table. I always had this bad taste in my mouth to allow them to use vampiric disciplines and thought it should be Arcanoi or nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T22:30:47-08:00","id":378734,"title":"","content":"Perhaps you were browsing the forums a little over a year ago and saw this thread? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/36196-wr20-risen-the-vampire-physical-disciplines\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/36196-wr20-risen-the-vampire-physical-disciplines\"> Wr20, Risen &amp; the Vampire Physical Disciplines - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/36196-wr20-risen-the-vampire-physical-disciplines\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/36196-wr20-risen-the-vampire-physical-disciplines </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> With Rich &amp;quot;Deadguy&amp;quot; Dansky blowing into the forums like a minor maelstrom, I thought this might be a good time to resurrect a topic from the old forums, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 01-23-2015, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T16:18:23-08:00","id":379598,"title":"","content":"I think it was on another site. If I am not mistaken, it was on a site that had a ton f homebrewed things for cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:25:01-07:00","id":446038,"title":"","content":"I assume the energies reanimating the dead in both cases are fundamentally similar. It's merely how they channel/distil that energy (blood/pathos), and how they got into that situation (Embrace/rising). Thus, they're Disciplines rather than Arcanoi. They also deal with the physical body rather than the soul/spirit, as Arcanoi usually do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:38:08-07:00","id":446053,"title":"","content":"@adambeyoncelowe We know that the Disciplines run off of Vitae. However, the Risen can use those Disciplines and use Pathos instead of Vitae. It explicitly states that in the Risen book. The thread was mainly to talk about someone who might have come up with Arcanoi that duplicate the effects of Potence, Celerity, Fortitude and Obfuscate. There was no official Arcanoi to do that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:48:57-07:00","id":446171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/374923-am-i-imagining-things?p=446053#post446053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@adambeyoncelowe We know that the Disciplines run off of Vitae. However, the Risen can use those Disciplines and use Pathos instead of Vitae. It explicitly states that in the Risen book. The thread was mainly to talk about someone who might have come up with Arcanoi that duplicate the effects of Potence, Celerity, Fortitude and Obfuscate. There was no official Arcanoi to do that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and that has been stated elsewhere in the thread, hence why I didn't repeat it. I was replying to marin's comment on how 'no one's sure' how the risen achieved the same results as the vampiric Disciplines. Just throwing in some conjecture on how those physical abilities are essentially the same, despite the different nature of the beings involved. I just forgot to quote that comment :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}